  "query_preview": "..Not a cloud to be found over Utah and southwest\nWyoming this morning with strong high pressure centered near the\nArizona/Nevada/Utah triple point. Some scattered high clouds over\nNevada will more into the area by early afternoon, but there is\nlittle else to speak of. With the strengthening of the ridge,\nmaxes should run a couple of degrees warmer than yesterday,\naveraging 10F above normal for this time of year.\n\nPersistence will be the name of the game tomorrow with the ridge\nmoving little. If anything, temperatures will be ever so slightly\nwarmer than today. The ridge axis will start to track east Sunday,\nand the resultant southerly flow will bring a couple of degrees of\nadditional warming for Sunday afternoon. \n\nAs the ridge continues east, this will open Utah and southwest\nWyoming up to a weak storm system late Monday into Tuesday. Weak\nis the key word here, as it will be accompanied by little if any\nshower activity and should drop high temperatures by a few degrees\nat most for Tuesday. The ridge will move back in for the middle to\nlatter part of the upcoming week, with guidance hinting at the\npotential of a more active pattern developing next weekend or\nearly next week.",
